# One line ending everywhere. The sources are edited on Windows and the exe is also built on macOS
# and Linux through build.sh; a repository that mixes the two shows whole files as changed when
# nobody has touched them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Whatever a checkout is told elsewhere, these keep LF: a carriage return in a shell script breaks
# bash, and it breaks it with an error that names the wrong line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Left byte for byte. Git must not go looking for line endings inside any of these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.rtf binary
*.msi binary
*.exe binary
